==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|ML.|en}} {{term|theosophia|lang=la}} < {{etyl|grc|en}} {{term|θεοσοφία||knowledge of things divine|lang=grc|tr=thesophia}} < {{term|θεός||god|tr=theos|lang=grc}} + {{term|σοφία||wisdom|tr=sophia|lang=grc}}.

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun|-|theosophies}}

# {{religion}} any of doctrines of religious philosophy and mysticism, claiming that knowledge of [[God]] can be attained through [[mystical]] [[insight]], spiritual ecstasy and that direct communication with [[transcendent]] world is possible

